{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3740,3880p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"                                 \"Stamped tree diverges from the compiled tree\"\n                                 {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\n                                  :pre-stamp-path pre-path\n                                  :stamped-path stamped-path\n                                  :field field\n                                  :pre-value pv\n                                  :stamped-value sv}))))))\n                (assoc acc stamped-path pre-path)\n                (map-indexed vector\n                             (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar\n                                  (:type pre)))))\n\n    (or (map? pre) (map? stamped))\n    (throw (ex-info \"Stamped tree diverges from the compiled tree\"\n                    {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\n                     :pre-stamp-path pre-path\n                     :stamped-path stamped-path}))\n\n    :else (if (= pre stamped)\n            acc\n            (throw (ex-info \"Stamped tree diverges from the compiled tree\"\n                            {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\n                             :pre-stamp-path pre-path\n                             :stamped-path stamped-path\n                             :pre-value pre\n                             :stamped-value stamped})))))\n\n\n(defn- cc3-oracle-binding\n  \"Bind each stamped oracle site id to its post-expansion C1 key\n   K = [origin root path] in the COMPILED (pre-stamp) tree.\n\n   Chronology (mob condition 2): `kernel-compile` compiles FIRST and\n   stamps by insertion afterward, so the stamped tree is a NEW tree.\n   Stamped paths are NOT pre-stamp paths (cc3 r2 item 1): the binding\n   translates each stamped site path through the explicit\n   `cc3-correspond` transformation mapping before combining it with\n   the pre-stamp root, and refuses a site whose mapped key is no\n   validated C1 occurrence. The origin is the admission coordinate\n   `kernel-compile` recorded WHEN ADMITTING the fixture and retained\n   with the compilation (`:admission-origin`, cc3 r2 item 2) — never\n   synthesized from content after compilation; a compilation without\n   a retained record refuses with `:rule :cc3-admission-record`, and\n   [:oracle/fixture <id>] is never minted.\"\n  [compiled]\n  (let [admission (:admission-origin compiled)]\n    (when-not (vm/occurrence-origin? admission)\n      (throw (ex-info \"Oracle binding requires the compilation's retained admission record\"\n                      {:rule :cc3-admission-record\n                       :admission admission})))\n    (let [ast (:compiled-ast compiled)\n          token (nth admission 2)\n          origin admission\n          projected (fn [tree-ast]\n                      (encoder/project\n                        (encoder/source-envelope :program token [tree-ast])))\n          {:keys [tree rows marked eligible]}\n          (let [p (projected ast)\n                t (first (:yin/batch p))\n                r (:yin/frontend-metadata p)]\n            {:tree t :rows r\n             :marked (into #{}\n                           (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\n                                 (map (fn [[o rr pth _ _]] [o rr pth])))\n                           r)\n             :eligible (into #{}\n                             (map (fn [[rr pth]] [origin rr pth]))\n                             (vm/application-occurrences t))})\n          ;; the POST-transformation tree verified separately (item 5)\n          {:keys [stamped-tree stamped-rows stamped-marked stamped-eligible]}\n          (let [p (projected (:ast compiled))\n                t (first (:yin/batch p))\n                r (:yin/frontend-metadata p)]\n            {:stamped-tree t :stamped-rows r\n             :stamped-marked (into #{}\n                                   (comp (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3)))\n                                         (map (fn [[o rr pth _ _]] [o rr pth])))\n                                   r)\n             :stamped-eligible (into #{}\n                                     (map (fn [[rr pth]] [origin rr pth]))\n                                     (vm/application-occurrences t))})\n          correspondence (cc3-correspond ast (:ast compiled) [] [] {})\n          ;; site entries are collected BEFORE any map is built: a\n          ;; duplicate site id refuses here, never overwrites an\n          ;; earlier occurrence in a map under construction (r3 F1)\n          site-entries (into []\n                             (comp (filter (fn [[_ node]]\n                                             (= :application (:type node))))\n                                   (keep (fn [[path node]]\n                                           (let [direct (cc3-stamp-site-id\n                                                          (second (:operands node)))\n                                                 inner (kernel-routed-call? node)\n                                                 routed (when inner\n                                                          (cc3-stamp-site-id\n                                                            (first (:operands inner))))]\n                                             (when-let [k (or direct routed)]\n                                               (let [pre-path (get correspondence\n                                                                   path\n                                                                   ::unmapped)]\n                                                 (when (= ::unmapped pre-path)\n                                                   (throw (ex-info\n                                                            \"Stamped site has no pre-stamp correspondence\"\n                                                            {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\n                                                             :site k\n                                                             :stamped-path path})))\n                                                 (let [key [origin (:root tree) pre-path]]\n                                                   (when-not (contains? marked key)\n                                                     (throw (ex-info\n                                                              \"Stamped site maps to no validated C1 occurrence\"\n                                                              {:rule :cc3-stamp-correspondence\n                                                               :site k\n                                                               :key key})))\n                                                   [k path key])))))))\n                             (cc3-walk (:ast compiled) [] []))\n          _ (when (not= (count site-entries)\n                        (count (into #{} (map first site-entries))))\n              (throw (ex-info \"Duplicate stamped site id\"\n                              {:rule :cc3-duplicate-stamp-site\n                               :sites (vec (sort (into []\n                                                       (comp (filter (fn [[_ n]]\n                                                                       (< 1 n)))\n                                                             (map first))\n                                                       (frequencies\n                                                         (map first\n                                                              site-entries)))))})))\n          stamped-paths (into {}\n                              (map (fn [[k path _key]] [k path]))\n                              site-entries)\n          stamped-sites (into {}\n                              (map (fn [[k _path key]] [k key]))\n                              site-entries)]\n      (when (not= (count stamped-sites)\n                  (count (into #{} (vals stamped-sites))))\n        (throw (ex-info \"Two stamped sites map to one pre-stamp occurrence\"\n                        {:rule :cc3-ambiguous-stamp-correspondence\n                         :binding stamped-sites})))\n      {:origin origin :tree tree :rows rows :marked marked\n       :eligible eligible :binding stamped-sites\n       :correspondence correspondence\n       :stamped-paths stamped-paths\n       :stamped-tree stamped-tree :stamped-rows stamped-rows\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r5.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md; git status --short --branch'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r5.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md; git status --short --branch'","aggregated_output":"# D1 continuation r5: amended fidelity and static replay pilot\n\nStatus: **partial; the full admission/replay gate is not complete**. This continues the append-only r1–r4 findings, including r4's historical class-strict refusal. Worktree mirror only; no canonical-collab promotion, commit, tagged execution, independent verifier result, or corpus record.\n\n## Fidelity amendment\n\n`yang.correspondence-text/profile` now includes `:fidelity-rule :fixed-jvm-integer-wrappers-v1`, so its content address differs from the r4 class-strict profile. Its numeric comparison permits equal Byte/Short/Integer/Long values via exact `long` comparison; all other admitted numeric leaves require same class and `.equals` (including Double NaN, signed zero and BigDecimal scale). Numeric dispatch occurs before generic `=`. Tests cover all four wrapper pairs, changed numeric coordinates, missing metadata, Long/BigInt, decimal scale, signed zero, NaN, collection kind and map/set iteration order. This is scoped to this experimental JVM profile and does not establish behavior for arbitrary programs.\n\nThe map mismatch path includes the map entry's actual key; capture failures name fixture, supplied admission scope, ordinal and input. The real-fixture test identifies r4's original mismatch precisely: `:beta-eq-false` forms `[15 2]` metadata entry 2 is `:line`, whose value is Integer before printing and Long after reading, with equal value. The amended capture **was observed to pass** on this fixture; it retains the supplied fresh admission coordinate and all four text captures. It does not change the historical r4 failure.\n\n## Producer-side static replay and reopen\n\nFor the one `:beta-eq-false` admission, the new test captures the original input, reads the captured text, recompiles, and compares its root, oracle canonical-source-hash, producer-derived site table, C1 metadata, site binding, stamped root/metadata and explicit stamped-to-unstamped correspondence with the original compilation. It validates both row trees and their application coverage; stamping adds two unmarked applications per wrapper, accounted separately from the C1 markers per the post-port cc3 test. It stores input, profile, expectations, and both canonical row closures in a file-backed store, closes and reopens it, checks all retained row bodies, and repeats the comparisons using fetched input/expectations. This runs only static compilation: no tagged machine, trace or verifier result. Test store is deleted after the test and is not durable publication of a corpus record.\n\nCrucial limit: `d1-check-reconstruction!` **shares** `kernel-stamp-sites`, `cc3-oracle-binding` and the oracle source-hash function with the producer. Thus its site table is not an independently re-derived declaration and the check is not an independent verifier or completed r5 gate. The exact executable dependency/expansion closure and runtime/profile compatibility are not pinned; no cross-host claim is made. A per-fixture replay test passes only that fixture and does not establish the entire corpus. The frozen v1 evidence remains unchanged.\n\n## Testing and remaining work\n\nTDD: the amended wrapper/NaN and profile-id tests first failed against the old class-strict implementation; the first replay test failed for missing helper; an attempted stamped-tree coverage assertion then failed because it incorrectly expected wrapper helpers to be marked, and was corrected to the post-port accounting. The diagnostic tests check the original `:line` key and retained scope/ordinal. The amended capture test passed 1 test / 7 assertions; the scoped capture-refusal test passed 1 test / 2 assertions; and the full pre/post-stamp reopened-store replay pilot passed 1 test / 6 assertions. The correspondence, text-profile and Clojure call-site battery passed 49 tests / 659 assertions. clj-kondo 2026.08.04 reported 0 errors and 0 warnings on the touched code/test files. Full oracle suite and tagged lanes were not run.\n\nStill required: independently derive the site declarations from compiled argument expressions; retain and pin the executable profile/interpreter/dependency and expansion closure; provide complete stage-specific refusal coverage and actual per-compilation gates for the corpus; retain the real record and recipe, companion and verification result under their proper ownership and bounds. The current successful pilot does not satisfy the r6 checkpoint of *all* gates complete. Row-lane-only remains the D1 restriction.\n## d1-correspondence...origin/master\n M test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r2.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r3.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r4.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r5.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md\n?? collab/yang-clojure/1794670000001-engineer-d1-correspondence-partial.findings.md\n?? src/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc\n?? src/cljc/yang/correspondence_text.clj\n?? test/yang/correspondence_test.cljc\n?? test/yang/correspondence_text_test.clj\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
